1
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:04,628
Hello, little space explorers!

2
00:00:05,008 --> 00:00:07,502
My name is Twinkle. I am a little star!

3
00:00:07,882 --> 00:00:10,669
Today, we are going on an amazing adventure...

4
00:00:11,049 --> 00:00:12,240
...to outer space!

5
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:14,779
Can you say it with me? Outer space!

6
00:00:16,959 --> 00:00:17,756
Wonderful!

7
00:00:19,136 --> 00:00:21,569
On our trip, we have four space missions.

8
00:00:21,949 --> 00:00:23,962
Mission one: the Solar System.

9
00:00:24,342 --> 00:00:26,896
Mission two: Earth, Moon, and Stars.

10
00:00:27,276 --> 00:00:30,048
Mission three: Astronomers and Astronauts.

11
00:00:30,428 --> 00:00:33,203
And mission four: What do we see in outer space?

12
00:00:33,583 --> 00:00:36,217
Are you ready? Let's climb into our rocket!

13
00:00:37,597 --> 00:00:41,451
Every astronaut checks the launch checklist. Let's check together!

14
00:00:41,831 --> 00:00:43,452
Oxygen... check!

15
00:00:43,832 --> 00:00:45,085
Weather... check!

16
00:00:45,465 --> 00:00:47,253
Engines ready... check!

17
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:49,413
Doors secure... check!

18
00:00:49,793 --> 00:00:52,225
We are go for launch! Count down with me!

19
00:00:52,605 --> 00:00:53,280
Five!

20
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:54,359
Four!

21
00:00:54,809 --> 00:00:55,439
Three!

22
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:56,473
Two!

23
00:00:56,923 --> 00:00:57,505
One!

24
00:00:57,955 --> 00:00:58,858
Blast off!

25
00:01:03,838 --> 00:01:06,018
Mission one... the Solar System!

26
00:01:08,198 --> 00:01:10,609
Whoosh! We are in space! Look all around.

27
00:01:10,989 --> 00:01:13,473
Everything around us is called the Universe.

28
00:01:13,853 --> 00:01:18,736
The Universe is everything! Every star, every planet... and even you and me!

29
00:01:19,116 --> 00:01:21,016
Here is our home, planet Earth.

30
00:01:21,396 --> 00:01:23,976
Here is the Sun and its family of planets.

31
00:01:24,356 --> 00:01:25,922
Here is our big galaxy...

32
00:01:26,302 --> 00:01:28,547
...and here are many, many more galaxies!

33
00:01:28,927 --> 00:01:34,137
Outer space is the big, big area beyond our Earth. It goes on and on and on!

34
00:01:35,517 --> 00:01:39,466
Ooh, it's getting warm! What is that big, bright ball? Can you guess?

35
00:01:42,916 --> 00:01:43,814
It's the Sun!

36
00:01:44,194 --> 00:01:47,598
Here's a surprise. The Sun is a star, just like me!

37
00:01:47,978 --> 00:01:50,963
It is a giant ball of hot, glowing gases.

38
00:01:51,343 --> 00:01:54,435
It is round, like a ball. We call this shape a sphere.

39
00:01:54,815 --> 00:01:57,493
Long ago, people called the Sun... Sol.

40
00:01:57,873 --> 00:02:01,458
That's why the Sun and its family are called the Solar System!

41
00:02:01,838 --> 00:02:06,201
Remember: never look straight at the Sun. It is much too bright for our eyes!

42
00:02:07,581 --> 00:02:09,268
How do you feel on a sunny day?

43
00:02:13,718 --> 00:02:15,741
Yes! We feel warm and cosy.

44
00:02:16,121 --> 00:02:19,913
The Sun sends light down to Earth. These are called sun rays.

45
00:02:20,293 --> 00:02:23,035
Sun rays fall on Earth, like golden rain!

46
00:02:23,415 --> 00:02:24,809
They make the air warmer...

47
00:02:25,189 --> 00:02:26,842
...and they dry up the wet streets!

48
00:02:27,222 --> 00:02:28,874
Let's sing our sunshine song!

49
00:02:29,254 --> 00:02:33,513
Shine, shine, Sun so bright! Warm the world with golden light!

50
00:02:33,893 --> 00:02:37,976
Shine, shine, high and round! Dry the puddles on the ground!

51
00:02:38,356 --> 00:02:39,052
Hooray!

52
00:02:40,432 --> 00:02:44,019
The Sun is not alone. It has a family of eight planets!

53
00:02:44,399 --> 00:02:47,118
The Sun is in the centre of the Solar System.

54
00:02:47,498 --> 00:02:48,798
Can you point to the Sun?

55
00:02:52,248 --> 00:02:54,358
Yes, right in the middle! Well done!

56
00:02:54,738 --> 00:02:59,114
The planets travel round and round the Sun. Their path is called an orbit.

57
00:02:59,494 --> 00:03:03,027
Let's meet the planets, in order from the Sun. Count with me!

58
00:03:03,407 --> 00:03:04,640
One: Mercury!

59
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,195
Two: Venus!

60
00:03:06,575 --> 00:03:07,648
Three: Earth!

61
00:03:08,028 --> 00:03:09,229
Four: Mars!

62
00:03:09,609 --> 00:03:10,860
Five: Jupiter!

63
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,380
Six: Saturn!

64
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,039
Seven: Uranus!

65
00:03:14,419 --> 00:03:15,675
Eight: Neptune!

66
00:03:16,055 --> 00:03:19,125
Many planets have moons that travel around them, too!

67
00:03:19,505 --> 00:03:22,960
Uh oh! One planet is hiding. Which planet is missing?

68
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:30,442
It's Earth, our home! Amazing!

69
00:03:31,822 --> 00:03:35,360
Our Sun is one star. But there are many, many more stars!

70
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:39,587
A galaxy is a giant group of stars and solar systems.

71
00:03:39,967 --> 00:03:43,022
Between them there is lots and lots of empty space.

72
00:03:43,402 --> 00:03:45,835
Our galaxy is called... the Milky Way!

73
00:03:46,215 --> 00:03:50,264
Our Earth and our Solar System live in the Milky Way. We are here!

74
00:03:50,644 --> 00:03:57,683
Scientists think there may be tens of billions of solar systems in our galaxy. That's more than we could ever count!

75
00:03:59,063 --> 00:04:00,756
Time for a quick space quiz!

76
00:04:01,136 --> 00:04:07,155
What is in the centre of the Solar System?

77
00:04:12,605 --> 00:04:14,462
It's B, the Sun! Excellent!

78
00:04:14,842 --> 00:04:21,008
What is the name of our galaxy?

79
00:04:26,458 --> 00:04:29,699
It's A, the Milky Way! Well done, space explorer!

80
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:35,176
How many planets travel around our Sun?

81
00:04:40,626 --> 00:04:42,383
B, eight planets! Super!

82
00:04:43,763 --> 00:04:45,557
Mission one... complete!

83
00:04:45,937 --> 00:04:48,478
Mission two... Earth, Moon, and Stars!

84
00:04:50,458 --> 00:04:52,121
What is the name of our planet?

85
00:04:56,571 --> 00:04:57,766
Earth! Brilliant!

86
00:04:58,146 --> 00:05:00,374
Earth is the third planet from the Sun.

87
00:05:00,754 --> 00:05:03,407
Let's count. One... two... three... Earth!

88
00:05:03,787 --> 00:05:07,973
Earth is our home. It has land, water, and air for us to breathe.

89
00:05:09,353 --> 00:05:12,986
Have you ever seen a globe? A globe is a model of the Earth.

90
00:05:13,366 --> 00:05:16,028
It is round, like a ball. It is a sphere!

91
00:05:16,408 --> 00:05:18,463
Let's pretend this torch is the Sun.

92
00:05:18,843 --> 00:05:20,112
Here is Pakistan.

93
00:05:20,492 --> 00:05:23,575
When Pakistan faces the Sun, it is daytime!

94
00:05:23,955 --> 00:05:28,438
The Earth spins around, like a top. This spinning is called rotation.

95
00:05:28,818 --> 00:05:32,086
It spins around a line through the middle, called the axis.

96
00:05:32,466 --> 00:05:34,612
The Earth spins around once every day.

97
00:05:34,993 --> 00:05:39,327
As Pakistan turns away from the Sun, it gets darker... and darker...

98
00:05:39,707 --> 00:05:41,065
Now it's night time!

99
00:05:41,445 --> 00:05:45,903
And when Pakistan turns back to the Sun... good morning! It's day again!

100
00:05:47,283 --> 00:05:49,373
Let's play a game. Day, or night?

101
00:05:49,753 --> 00:05:54,073
Children are playing in the park, and the Sun is shining. Day, or night?

102
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:58,107
Day!

103
00:05:58,487 --> 00:06:02,336
An owl says hoo hoo, under the Moon and stars. Day, or night?

104
00:06:05,786 --> 00:06:06,436
Night!

105
00:06:06,816 --> 00:06:10,349
We eat breakfast and get ready for school. Day, or night?

106
00:06:13,799 --> 00:06:14,382
Day!

107
00:06:14,762 --> 00:06:18,709
We are fast asleep in bed, tucked in tight. Day, or night?

108
00:06:22,159 --> 00:06:23,708
Night! You are so clever!

109
00:06:24,088 --> 00:06:29,880
In the day, we see the Sun and the blue sky. At night, we can see the Moon and the stars.

110
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:32,873
What can we see in the night sky?

111
00:06:36,323 --> 00:06:37,751
Stars... and the Moon!

112
00:06:38,131 --> 00:06:39,863
Let's zoom in close to the Moon.

113
00:06:40,243 --> 00:06:42,429
The Moon's surface has tall mountains...

114
00:06:42,809 --> 00:06:43,931
...deep valleys...

115
00:06:44,311 --> 00:06:45,615
...old volcanoes...

116
00:06:45,995 --> 00:06:48,592
...and lots of dusty holes, called craters!

117
00:06:48,972 --> 00:06:51,144
We can see the Moon with just our eyes.

118
00:06:51,524 --> 00:06:55,791
But with a telescope, or binoculars, it looks much bigger and closer!

119
00:06:57,171 --> 00:06:59,826
Have you noticed that the Moon seems to change shape?

120
00:07:00,206 --> 00:07:03,421
The Moon travels around the Earth. This is its orbit.

121
00:07:03,801 --> 00:07:08,819
The Moon has no light of its own. It reflects light from the Sun, like a mirror!

122
00:07:09,199 --> 00:07:13,198
As the Moon goes around us, we see different parts of its sunny side.

123
00:07:13,578 --> 00:07:15,283
Sometimes a thin crescent...

124
00:07:15,663 --> 00:07:17,076
...sometimes half a Moon...

125
00:07:17,456 --> 00:07:19,626
...and sometimes a big, round, full Moon!

126
00:07:20,006 --> 00:07:22,758
Which one is the full Moon? A, B, or C?

127
00:07:27,208 --> 00:07:29,591
C! The big round one! Fantastic!

128
00:07:30,971 --> 00:07:36,624
Long ago, in nineteen sixty-nine, a very brave astronaut flew all the way to the Moon.

129
00:07:37,004 --> 00:07:38,738
His name was Neil Armstrong.

130
00:07:39,118 --> 00:07:41,757
He was the very first person to walk on the Moon!

131
00:07:42,137 --> 00:07:45,325
He explored the Moon, and left his footprints in the dust.

132
00:07:45,705 --> 00:07:49,042
Bounce, bounce! Walking on the Moon is called a moon walk!

133
00:07:49,422 --> 00:07:52,245
Can you do a moon walk? Bounce, bounce, bounce!

134
00:07:56,695 --> 00:07:57,984
Great moon walking!

135
00:07:59,364 --> 00:08:03,681
Look at all the stars! They look like glitter, sprinkled across the sky.

136
00:08:04,061 --> 00:08:06,158
Twinkle... sparkle... shine!

137
00:08:06,538 --> 00:08:08,827
Can we touch a star? What do you think?

138
00:08:13,277 --> 00:08:19,688
No, we can't! Stars are hot balls of gas. They are very, very hot, and very, very far away!

139
00:08:20,068 --> 00:08:22,575
Don't worry. I'm a friendly cartoon star!

140
00:08:22,955 --> 00:08:27,728
Here is a secret. Stars are always in the sky, even in the daytime!

141
00:08:28,108 --> 00:08:31,454
In the day, the Sun is so bright that we cannot see them.

142
00:08:31,834 --> 00:08:35,678
When the Sun goes down, the dark night lets the stars shine through!

143
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:41,971
Some groups of stars make pictures in the sky. These are called constellations.

144
00:08:42,351 --> 00:08:45,438
Watch the stars join up. What picture do you see?

145
00:08:49,888 --> 00:08:56,511
It looks like a big spoon! People call it the Big Dipper. It is part of a star picture called the Great Bear.

146
00:08:56,891 --> 00:08:59,377
Whoosh! Did you see that? A shooting star!

147
00:08:59,757 --> 00:09:06,687
A shooting star is not really a star. It is a tiny space rock that glows as it zooms through the sky.

148
00:09:07,067 --> 00:09:12,226
If a space rock falls all the way down and lands on Earth, we call it a meteorite!

149
00:09:13,606 --> 00:09:17,612
On a dark, clear night, far away from bright city lights, look up!

150
00:09:17,992 --> 00:09:22,190
You may see a dusty, white band of stars stretching across the sky.

151
00:09:22,570 --> 00:09:24,711
That is our galaxy, the Milky Way!

152
00:09:25,091 --> 00:09:28,287
It is made of stars, dust, and clouds of gas.

153
00:09:28,667 --> 00:09:35,143
It has hundreds of billions of stars! And it is just one of billions of galaxies in the Universe!

154
00:09:36,523 --> 00:09:41,161
True or false? Thumbs up for true. Thumbs down for false. Ready?

155
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:43,687
The Earth spins around once every day.

156
00:09:48,137 --> 00:09:49,329
True! Thumbs up!

157
00:09:49,709 --> 00:09:51,502
Stars go away in the daytime.

158
00:09:55,952 --> 00:10:00,544
False! The stars are still there. The Sun is just too bright for us to see them.

159
00:10:00,924 --> 00:10:02,465
The Moon makes its own light.

160
00:10:06,915 --> 00:10:09,545
False! The Moon reflects light from the Sun.

161
00:10:09,925 --> 00:10:13,146
When our side of Earth faces the Sun, it is daytime.

162
00:10:17,596 --> 00:10:18,861
True! Amazing!

163
00:10:20,241 --> 00:10:22,036
Mission two... complete!

164
00:10:22,416 --> 00:10:25,253
Mission three... Astronomers and Astronauts!

165
00:10:27,233 --> 00:10:31,548
People who study space use a special science. It's called astronomy!

166
00:10:31,928 --> 00:10:39,878
Astronomy is the science of outer space. It studies the Sun, the Moon, stars, comets, planets, and galaxies.

167
00:10:40,258 --> 00:10:42,933
People who study space are called astronomers.

168
00:10:43,313 --> 00:10:46,639
People have been studying the sky for thousands of years!

169
00:10:48,019 --> 00:10:50,201
Let's meet three famous astronomers!

170
00:10:50,581 --> 00:10:56,185
This is Galileo Galilei. He built telescopes, and used them to look at the night sky.

171
00:10:56,565 --> 00:11:01,754
This is Isaac Newton. He discovered gravity. Gravity is an invisible pull.

172
00:11:02,134 --> 00:11:07,596
Gravity makes an apple fall down from a tree... and it keeps the planets going around the Sun!

173
00:11:07,976 --> 00:11:14,661
The Sun's pull reaches far out into space, all around it. This is called a gravitational field.

174
00:11:15,041 --> 00:11:21,459
This is Edwin Hubble. A giant space telescope is named after him: the Hubble Space Telescope!

175
00:11:21,839 --> 00:11:26,530
It floats in space, and takes amazing pictures of stars and galaxies.

176
00:11:26,910 --> 00:11:31,760
Who built telescopes to look at the night sky? Galileo, Newton, or Hubble?

177
00:11:36,210 --> 00:11:38,027
Galileo! Super memory!

178
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:42,492
Hi, everyone! I'm Captain Zoe. I'm an astronaut!

179
00:11:42,872 --> 00:11:45,841
Hello, Captain Zoe! What do astronauts do?

180
00:11:46,221 --> 00:11:49,450
Astronauts travel into space in rockets and spaceships.

181
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:54,645
We visit space to collect information, for scientists and astronomers to study.

182
00:11:55,025 --> 00:11:58,155
And sometimes, we fix spaceships while we are in space!

183
00:11:58,535 --> 00:12:02,514
Welcome to my space station! Let's press the buttons. Beep, boop!

184
00:12:02,894 --> 00:12:05,649
You can build a space station in your classroom, too!

185
00:12:07,029 --> 00:12:10,169
Living in space is very different from living on Earth.

186
00:12:10,549 --> 00:12:14,654
On Earth, there is air all around us. But in space, there is no air!

187
00:12:15,034 --> 00:12:17,262
So how do astronauts breathe in space?

188
00:12:21,712 --> 00:12:24,767
We need oxygen! So we wear a special space suit.

189
00:12:25,147 --> 00:12:27,580
My backpack holds air, for me to breathe.

190
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:32,375
My helmet has a dark visor, to protect my eyes from the Sun's glare.

191
00:12:32,755 --> 00:12:38,134
My suit is big, thick, and bulky. It keeps me safe from the Sun's heat, and from the cold.

192
00:12:38,514 --> 00:12:40,941
And my heavy boots help me walk on the Moon!

193
00:12:41,321 --> 00:12:44,606
In space, nothing has weight, so everything floats! Wheee!

194
00:12:44,986 --> 00:12:50,715
What helps an astronaut breathe?

195
00:12:55,165 --> 00:12:57,408
B! A backpack of air! Well done!

196
00:12:58,788 --> 00:13:01,212
Captain Zoe, how do you sleep in space?

197
00:13:01,592 --> 00:13:05,531
We sleep in sleeping bags that are tied down, so we don't float away!

198
00:13:05,911 --> 00:13:08,169
How do you think astronauts drink in space?

199
00:13:12,619 --> 00:13:16,733
We can't drink from a cup. The water would float away in wobbly bubbles!

200
00:13:17,113 --> 00:13:19,776
So we drink through a straw, from a plastic pouch.

201
00:13:20,156 --> 00:13:25,847
Space food is special, too. Most of it is freeze dried, or packed tight with the air sucked out.

202
00:13:26,227 --> 00:13:31,966
Some food is a powder in a pouch, a bit like baby food. We add water, and suck it out. Yum!

203
00:13:32,346 --> 00:13:36,548
Some space food is sticky, so it sticks to the plate and doesn't float away!

204
00:13:37,928 --> 00:13:40,103
Every astronaut keeps a log book!

205
00:13:40,483 --> 00:13:44,875
It has a cover with your name, a launch checklist, and a space chart of the planets.

206
00:13:45,255 --> 00:13:49,842
Now it's your turn! Imagine you are filling in an astronaut application.

207
00:13:50,222 --> 00:13:52,042
Why do you want to be an astronaut?

208
00:13:57,492 --> 00:13:59,811
And if you went to space, what would you do?

209
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:09,203
What wonderful ideas! You would make a fantastic astronaut!

210
00:14:10,583 --> 00:14:12,453
Mission three... complete!

211
00:14:12,833 --> 00:14:15,565
Mission four... What do we see in outer space?

212
00:14:17,545 --> 00:14:20,837
What else can we see in outer space? Look, a satellite!

213
00:14:21,217 --> 00:14:24,494
A satellite is a spacecraft that is sent into space.

214
00:14:24,874 --> 00:14:28,587
It collects information, and sends it back to Earth by radio.

215
00:14:28,967 --> 00:14:33,469
Satellites send TV programmes and information all around the world!

216
00:14:34,849 --> 00:14:38,562
How do astronauts and things get into space? With rockets!

217
00:14:38,942 --> 00:14:41,764
Rockets carry astronauts and things into space.

218
00:14:42,144 --> 00:14:47,354
Only rocket engines are strong enough and fast enough to get a spacecraft into space.

219
00:14:47,734 --> 00:14:54,559
Fuel burns inside the engine. It rushes out of the bottom, called the nozzle, and pushes the rocket up!

220
00:14:54,939 --> 00:14:58,353
It's just like blowing a paper wrapper off a straw. Whoosh!

221
00:14:58,733 --> 00:15:00,058
This is a space shuttle.

222
00:15:00,438 --> 00:15:06,401
The space shuttle could blast off just like a rocket, and come back to Earth like a giant glider!

223
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:10,870
When it came back through the air around Earth, it got very, very hot!

224
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:16,958
And this is a space rover. It's a robot car that drives around and explores other worlds!

225
00:15:18,338 --> 00:15:23,012
We have one Moon. But did you know there are hundreds of moons in our Solar System?

226
00:15:23,392 --> 00:15:27,276
Let's have a planet parade, and learn a fun fact about each planet!

227
00:15:27,656 --> 00:15:32,554
Mercury is the closest planet to the Sun. It is also the smallest planet.

228
00:15:32,934 --> 00:15:41,006
Venus is the hottest planet. It is the brightest planet in our sky. If you know where to look, you can see it with just your eyes!

229
00:15:41,386 --> 00:15:46,180
Earth is our home. It has more water than land. Look at the big blue oceans!

230
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:53,721
Mars is the red planet. It has the biggest volcano in the Solar System. It is called Olympus Mons!

231
00:15:54,101 --> 00:16:04,247
Jupiter is the largest planet of all! Its four biggest moons are named after Galileo. They are called Io, Europa, Ganymede and Callisto.

232
00:16:04,627 --> 00:16:09,555
Saturn is a giant planet, made of gas. It is the second largest planet.

233
00:16:09,935 --> 00:16:19,735
Saturn has beautiful rings, made of ice. Some pieces are as big as houses, and some are as tiny as dust! Saturn has lots of moons, too.

234
00:16:20,115 --> 00:16:26,381
Uranus likes to be different! It is blue-green, and it rolls around on its side, like a barrel!

235
00:16:26,761 --> 00:16:33,052
Neptune is the farthest planet from the Sun. It is big, almost four times as wide as Earth!

236
00:16:33,432 --> 00:16:37,450
And far, far away, there are little dwarf planets too, like Pluto!

237
00:16:38,830 --> 00:16:41,409
Look! What is that, with a long, glowing tail?

238
00:16:44,859 --> 00:16:45,866
It's a comet!

239
00:16:46,246 --> 00:16:51,641
A comet is like a big, dirty snowball, made of ice, frozen gases, and dust.

240
00:16:52,021 --> 00:16:55,531
It travels around the Sun, on a long, stretched-out path.

241
00:16:55,911 --> 00:17:01,387
When it comes close to the Sun, it warms up, and makes a glowing cloud and a long tail!

242
00:17:01,767 --> 00:17:06,371
Remember, a space rock that falls down to Earth is called a meteorite.

243
00:17:06,751 --> 00:17:10,067
And a big rock floating in space is called an asteroid.

244
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:13,499
Hmm. Do aliens live in space?

245
00:17:13,879 --> 00:17:17,669
Nobody has ever found an alien. But it's fun to imagine!

246
00:17:18,049 --> 00:17:20,533
If you were an alien, what would your name be?

247
00:17:24,983 --> 00:17:26,517
Which planet would you live on?

248
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:34,191
And what would you eat? Moon cheese? Star sprinkles?

249
00:17:38,641 --> 00:17:40,466
Ha ha! What a funny alien!

250
00:17:41,846 --> 00:17:43,732
Hooray! It's Solar System Day!

251
00:17:44,112 --> 00:17:49,519
Children dress up as the Sun and the planets, and tell everyone a fact about themselves.

252
00:17:49,899 --> 00:17:51,722
I am the Sun! I am a star!

253
00:17:52,102 --> 00:17:54,792
I am Earth! I have blue oceans!

254
00:17:55,172 --> 00:17:57,816
I am Saturn! I have beautiful rings!

255
00:17:58,196 --> 00:17:59,884
Which planet would you like to be?

256
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:07,279
Then everyone sings the Solar System song together!

257
00:18:10,159 --> 00:18:12,714
Revision time! Let's play: What is this?

258
00:18:16,244 --> 00:18:17,277
A space shuttle!

259
00:18:20,807 --> 00:18:21,592
A planet!

260
00:18:25,122 --> 00:18:26,181
An astronaut!

261
00:18:29,711 --> 00:18:30,441
The Moon!

262
00:18:33,971 --> 00:18:34,706
The Sun!

263
00:18:38,236 --> 00:18:39,230
An asteroid!

264
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:43,861
A space rover!

265
00:18:47,391 --> 00:18:48,161
Stars!

266
00:18:51,691 --> 00:18:52,560
A rocket!

267
00:18:56,090 --> 00:18:57,048
A telescope!

268
00:19:00,578 --> 00:19:01,453
A satellite!

269
00:19:04,983 --> 00:19:05,828
A comet!

270
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:08,692
You know all your space words! Amazing!

271
00:19:10,072 --> 00:19:12,109
Let's remember everything we learned!

272
00:19:12,489 --> 00:19:16,060
The Universe is everything. Outer space goes on and on!

273
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:21,876
The Sun is a star, a hot glowing ball. It is in the centre of the Solar System.

274
00:19:22,256 --> 00:19:29,216
Eight planets orbit the Sun. Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune!

275
00:19:29,596 --> 00:19:32,650
We live on planet Earth, in the Milky Way galaxy.

276
00:19:33,030 --> 00:19:38,008
Earth spins on its axis. Facing the Sun is day. Facing away is night.

277
00:19:38,388 --> 00:19:41,771
The Moon has craters, and it reflects light from the Sun.

278
00:19:42,151 --> 00:19:45,944
Stars are hot balls of gas, and they are always in the sky.

279
00:19:46,324 --> 00:19:51,130
Astronomers study space. Astronauts travel to space, in space suits!

280
00:19:51,510 --> 00:19:56,529
Rockets, satellites, comets, and meteorites. Space is full of wonders!

281
00:19:57,909 --> 00:20:02,707
It's time for the big final quiz! Listen carefully, and shout out your answer!

282
00:20:03,087 --> 00:20:08,542
I am the farthest planet from the Sun. Who am I?

283
00:20:13,992 --> 00:20:15,495
Neptune! Excellent!

284
00:20:15,875 --> 00:20:20,141
I have got the oceans. Who am I?

285
00:20:25,591 --> 00:20:26,816
Earth! Well done!

286
00:20:27,196 --> 00:20:31,842
I am the largest planet. Who am I?

287
00:20:37,292 --> 00:20:38,829
Jupiter! Amazing!

288
00:20:39,209 --> 00:20:44,625
I have big, beautiful rings around me. Who am I?

289
00:20:50,075 --> 00:20:51,252
Saturn! Super!

290
00:20:51,632 --> 00:20:56,213
I am the hottest planet. Who am I?

291
00:21:01,663 --> 00:21:02,997
Venus! Brilliant!

292
00:21:03,377 --> 00:21:08,026
I roll around on my side. Who am I?

293
00:21:13,476 --> 00:21:15,098
Uranus! Fantastic!

294
00:21:15,478 --> 00:21:19,657
I am the red planet. Who am I?

295
00:21:25,107 --> 00:21:26,424
Mars! Excellent!

296
00:21:26,804 --> 00:21:33,157
I am the smallest planet, and the closest to the Sun. Who am I?

297
00:21:38,607 --> 00:21:40,134
Mercury! Well done!

298
00:21:40,514 --> 00:21:46,370
Who was the first person to walk on the Moon?

299
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:53,767
Neil Armstrong! Amazing!

300
00:21:54,147 --> 00:21:59,034
What do astronauts need to breathe in space?

301
00:22:04,484 --> 00:22:06,024
Oxygen! Super!

302
00:22:06,404 --> 00:22:10,907
When your side of the Earth faces away from the Sun, is it day or night?

303
00:22:16,357 --> 00:22:17,582
Night! Brilliant!

304
00:22:17,962 --> 00:22:21,881
What is a shooting star?

305
00:22:27,331 --> 00:22:29,347
A tiny space rock! Excellent!

306
00:22:29,727 --> 00:22:34,095
Wow! You know so much about outer space! You are a super space explorer!

307
00:22:35,475 --> 00:22:38,963
Mission four... complete! All our missions are complete!

308
00:22:39,343 --> 00:22:41,995
You did an amazing job, space explorers!

309
00:22:42,375 --> 00:22:44,588
Here is your Super Space Explorer medal!

310
00:22:44,968 --> 00:22:49,997
Ask your teacher about our space worksheets. And build your own space station at school!

311
00:22:50,377 --> 00:22:54,200
Tonight, look up at the sky. Can you find the Moon and the stars?

312
00:22:54,580 --> 00:22:56,794
Keep exploring, and keep discovering!

313
00:22:57,174 --> 00:22:59,688
Goodbye, little stars! See you next time!

